{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn","id":1102926,"title":"Red Rage of Terrible Revenge - Damage Per Turn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-12T15:06:54-07:00","id":1102926,"title":"Red Rage of Terrible Revenge - Damage Per Turn","content":"So I remember this ability from 1e, and in that it was pretty powerful. Looking over it now, it looks much the same - with a new addition: It inflicts 1 lethal per turn to the user so long as the user is using it. I'm a bit curious if people feel this works with this nerf? I personally am not sure I could use it outside of when it's catch came up (and even then, if you rolled say - one or two successes, you are probably better off without it).<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten the chance to test it out yet though - and am curious if others have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T17:54:49-07:00","id":1102964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn#post1102926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I remember this ability from 1e, and in that it was pretty powerful. Looking over it now, it looks much the same - with a new addition: It inflicts 1 lethal per turn to the user so long as the user is using it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also lost the &quot;it only works in combat and you lose viable access to defensive tactics that aren't blocking or tanking hits&quot; aspect. The general brevity in turn-count of 2e combat is worth remembering, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T18:00:08-07:00","id":1102965,"title":"","content":"Here's the thing. RRoTR gains +1 Strength, Initiative and Armor per success. That per success bit is huge. Between goblin vows, Contracts, kiths and merits, Changelings get insanely big dice pools. We're talking about easily getting 25 dice to activate RRoTR with the right set up. Think about that a tick. That's around 8 successes. +8 Strength. +8 Init. +8 Armor. +Wyrd/2 Stamina. +1 lethal damage. <br /> <br /> With that armor, you will not be taking damage other than the 1 lethal per turn. With both seeming clauses, you'll be able to last on your feet for a long time and dish out some damge. All in all, most combats will be over long before you run out of health. With one dot of Bounty, that'll get you three blushberries, healing 6 damge. <br /> <br /> There's a lot of power in this contract. The problem is that lots of changeling doesn't really come down to combat. Most antagonists are very subtle, because they know they could lose in a direct fight. Loyalists sneak in, fetches go crazy, Huntsmen excell at disguises, onerois come into your mind while asleep, hobs deal in the markets with their own magics, arcadian ghosts are ephemeral, and the Gentry themselves? Well....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T03:31:10-07:00","id":1103067,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1102964#post1102964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also lost the &quot;it only works in combat and you lose viable access to defensive tactics that aren't blocking or tanking hits&quot; aspect. The general brevity in turn-count of 2e combat is worth remembering, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, I would think it is an even worse option to use out of combat. Though at the very least out of combat I could see one routinely using goblin fruit to offset the damage, if you had it about.<br /> <br /> The Brevity in turn count is, actually, part of the reason I don't immediately dismiss the contract outright for it's drawbacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1102965#post1102965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing. RRoTR gains +1 Strength, Initiative and Armor per success. That per success bit is huge. Between goblin vows, Contracts, kiths and merits, Changelings get insanely big dice pools. We're talking about easily getting 25 dice to activate RRoTR with the right set up. Think about that a tick. That's around 8 successes. +8 Strength. +8 Init. +8 Armor. +Wyrd/2 Stamina. +1 lethal damage.<br /> <br /> With that armor, you will not be taking damage other than the 1 lethal per turn. With both seeming clauses, you'll be able to last on your feet for a long time and dish out some damge. All in all, most combats will be over long before you run out of health. With one dot of Bounty, that'll get you three blushberries, healing 6 damge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... seems like a lot of work to make a 5 dot contract useful though. While I don't deny the 'per success' bit is a huge <i>potential</i> benefit, it's also a huge potential detriment as well. Not everyone who needs a combat contract is going to have a strength 5, survival 5, Wyrd 3, with merits and other contracts to enhance that - and when your swinging a dice pool of 7-10 around (The average changeling dice pool I've seen for a contract), the odds of hitting a non-exceptional success become a lot higher. Is it really worth a lethal a turn, 3 glamour, and an instant action when all you might get is +2 Strength, Initiative, and Armor?<br /> <br /> As a side note, you'll have to forgive me but... bounty? I went and looked through the playtest, and while I found Harvest (which is not what you are suggesting, it seems) I could not find 'bounty' anywhere. That sounds like a cool merit to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1102965#post1102965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of power in this contract. The problem is that lots of changeling doesn't really come down to combat. Most antagonists are very subtle, because they know they could lose in a direct fight. Loyalists sneak in, fetches go crazy, Huntsmen excell at disguises, onerois come into your mind while asleep, hobs deal in the markets with their own magics, arcadian ghosts are ephemeral, and the Gentry themselves? Well....</div> </div> </div> </div>Or when combat -does- come into play, it's rarely so direct as this contract seems designed to be. Things like changeling hours, leaping towards nightfall, and the myriad of methods in which a fae entity can make another person suffer the blind tilt make the number of counters an antagonist might use to a good roll with this seem... rather myriad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T06:15:35-07:00","id":1103100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1103067#post1103067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That... seems like a lot of work to make a 5 dot contract useful though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Far less than you think. For example, lets say I take &quot;Punishing Summer&quot; as a Goblin Vow; you'll get something like that with the second dot of Summer Mantle anyways. Using medial benefits (the cost is easier to pay than major), I can get +3 to all Strength rolls, and +5 to Survival checks. If I'm working RRoTR, I probably also have Might of the Terrible Brute, for +Wyrd to my strength. Lets say a Wyrd of 3 for the sake of simplicity. Starting Strength of 3, starting Survival of 3. All this within grasp of a slightly experienced character.<br /> <br /> Strength 3 + Survival 3 + Wyrd 3 + MotTB 3 + GV 3 + GV 5 + wp = 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 5 + 3 = 23 dice.<br /> <br /> And this is not involving any kith bonuses, extremely high stats, and only uses one other Contract someone taking RRoTR should have anyways. And most of those goblin vow bonuses are things a combat focused character wants to have in the first place. This is not min-maxing. Hells, I haven't even touched on using Kith or Seeming bonuses, exploiting specialties, bonuses from other synergetic Contracts, and more.<br /> <br /> Huge dice pools are what changelings do.<br /> <br /> EDIT - oh, yeah! And don't forget Embracing the Wyrd! That's an extra 3 dice here. There's also Shattering the Mask for some auto-successes on contracts if you're in a pinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-13-2017, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T06:38:13-07:00","id":1103110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1103067#post1103067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a side note, you'll have to forgive me but... bounty? I went and looked through the playtest, and while I found Harvest (which is not what you are suggesting, it seems) I could not find 'bounty' anywhere. That sounds like a cool merit to have.</div> </div> </div> </div> The compiled pdf is actually missing some bits of information. Get the latest Chapter 3 stand alone pdf. It has some merits and other bits that aren't in the compiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:40:52-07:00","id":1103170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1103100#post1103100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Far less than you think. For example, lets say I take &quot;Punishing Summer&quot; as a Goblin Vow; you'll get something like that with the second dot of Summer Mantle anyways. Using medial benefits (the cost is easier to pay than major), I can get +3 to all Strength rolls, and +5 to Survival checks. If I'm working RRoTR, I probably also have Might of the Terrible Brute, for +Wyrd to my strength. Lets say a Wyrd of 3 for the sake of simplicity. Starting Strength of 3, starting Survival of 3. All this within grasp of a slightly experienced character.<br /> <br /> Strength 3 + Survival 3 + Wyrd 3 + MotTB 3 + GV 3 + GV 5 + wp = 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 5 + 3 = 23 dice.<br /> <br /> And this is not involving any kith bonuses, extremely high stats, and only uses one other Contract someone taking RRoTR should have anyways. And most of those goblin vow bonuses are things a combat focused character wants to have in the first place. This is not min-maxing. Hells, I haven't even touched on using Kith or Seeming bonuses, exploiting specialties, bonuses from other synergetic Contracts, and more.<br /> <br /> Huge dice pools are what changelings do.<br /> <br /> EDIT - oh, yeah! And don't forget Embracing the Wyrd! That's an extra 3 dice here. There's also Shattering the Mask for some auto-successes on contracts if you're in a pinch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. Okay, will confess - a bit easier to do than I had thought. However: You are still expending a considerable amount of IC effort to manage. If you include embracing the Wyrd, that's 4 willpower spent, which also tends to mean 4 turns spent, to activate it. In my opinion, this would not be a problem - preparing a contract in anticipation of a fight can definately happen - but the lethal damage tends to make it a very -hard- thing to time.<br /> <br /> Oh! Thank you, I'll look over there.<br /> <br /> Edit: Would you mind sending me a link? I can't find it. ;(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 06-13-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T18:44:08-07:00","id":1103353,"title":"","content":"Well, considering that the medial Goblin Vows last for a week by default, I'm not sure you're right about the willpower cost or timing. You keep it active at the start of the week, or once on Saturday/Sunday, then get the bonus all week. Embracing the Wyrd is reflexive, but unnecessary in this case anyways. I just mentioned it offhand as a way to pump up your pool even higher if desired. The only wp is really coming from using the Contract, and hopefully, with all the strength bonuses, you'll be getting Inspired and getting your willpower.<br /> <br /> The timing is really down to just one turn to activate RRoTR, which happens irregardless of the rest. Depending on the game, that could be finicky, or it could be fine. <br /> <br /> As for the link? I'll just give you mine from my drive... <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3Ygaqyqv6i7d2pabmYxRlZ6d00/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B3Y...ew?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T19:58:30-07:00","id":1103363,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Far as the week default, that tends to be prep work. If you know your going to get into a fight in the next 4 days, and prepare it - you might alleviate the immediate need. But for the most part I don't really see people routinely having those specific goblin vows and arrangements set up before hand, and them having to set it up once they knew they'd need it? While that -can- be known as 'a few days from now' most of the time that knowledge comes very, very suddenly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T04:41:29-07:00","id":1103441,"title":"","content":"I have a PC that maintains three goblin vows at all times. If its something you're interested in, there's little reason not to, other than fear of failing a task. Once the week is up, I re-establish it with a willpower point and a new pledge. Our hollow has a Route Zero, so I can replenish the spent willpower at the beginning of the day as well. I see no reason you couldn't have it active if you didnt'. For an ogre? Having Strength bonus constantly active is practically a given, if you ask me.<br /> <br /> With giant dice pools, its also pretty easy to get Inspired from exceptional success all the time. Not to farm beats, but to farm willpower as necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-14-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T16:06:04-07:00","id":1103640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1102926-red-rage-of-terrible-revenge-damage-per-turn?p=1103441#post1103441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For an ogre? Having Strength bonus constantly active is practically a given, if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definately can't argue with that one. It's the survival being boosted before hand that is the unlikely one<br /> <br /> Alright - so I'm not really convinced that the contract is worth it's exuberant cost, given the sheer amount of effort it takes to make it pliable. That said, I do believe that without the damage it's potentially very OP, so me and my ST changed it to bashing instead of lethal. We'll see how that works out, and if it comes off as too much then we may return it to lethal.<br /> <br /> That said, thank you for the assistance MCN - if nothing else, this discussion has definitely highlighted some of the advantages of goblin vows for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T17:40:29-07:00","id":1103669,"title":"","content":"I think my problem with the self-inflicted automatic damage last time I looked at the previewed Red Rage was more how it seems a disproportionate cost in relation to the requisites of other five dot contracts, its effectiveness with the assumption of an easily stacked deck nonwithstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T07:33:52-07:00","id":1103804,"title":"","content":"Either way, I prefer other five dot contracts anyways. Tying Knots of Fate (dear god), Phantonm Glory (elemental clause pluse Elemental Combat 5, anyone? Scary as hell), Chrysalis (better for shapeshifting abilities than actual mechanics), Paralyzing Shudder (literally crippled), Leaping Toward Nightfall is pretty amazing in a number of situations. Hedgewall all but lets you make a castle in the middle of the hedge. Which is awesome. Animate Device, when used with some prep time, can turn an entire environment against another. How cool is it to be invading a traitor's home and turning the home against them?<br /> <br /> RRoTR is joined by Thief of Reason and Vision of Fortune\u2019s Favor as probably the worst of 5-dot Contracts. Thief of Reason relies on having Clarity, which makes the main changeling antagonists (hobs, gentry, huntsmen) ineligable for being targetted, and Paralyzing Shudder is just as effective in shutting someone down, not to mention its just cruel to use. VoFF is a well done &quot;rewind time&quot; ability, but it suffers from the simple fact that rearranging one turn when CofD devolves to rocket tag is still unlikely to have a huge benefit. Activating this when faced with a ranged weapon or Contract / high Speed attacker (Shudder, Thief of Reason, etc) doesn't actually change the outcome. You need to pair it with another rocket-tag ability, and even then, there's issues with initiative orders.<br /> <br /> I also find it strange that pretty much all the high level contracts seem to revolve around combat in some way. Animate Device and Tying the Knots of Fate seem to be exceptions (though they can apply to combat with devistating effectiveness). Says something about the game, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}